  "classesText": "Right answers by class\n\nFor each answer-key class: how many reviews the model got right (recall). Small classes swing on one or two reviews.\n\nPositive\n48 of 50 \u00b7 96.0% \u00b7 2 wrong\nNeutral\n17 of 50 \u00b7 34.0% \u00b7 33 wrong\nNegative\n45 of 50 \u00b7 90.0% \u00b7 5 wrong\nRight\nWrong\n\nWhen the model says a class, how often it is right (precision): Positive 84.2% \u00b7 Neutral 73.9% \u00b7 Negative 64.3%\n\nEach class is a third of this sample. The whole file is 88.5% positive, 2.1% neutral and 9.3% negative. Re-weighted to that mix, precision would be about: Positive 99.4% \u00b7 Neutral 14.5% \u00b7 Negative 88.6%, and accuracy about 94.1% (a rough estimate from this sample)."
